    "source": "DOCS/CHANGELOG.md",
    "present": true,
    "heading": "v1.34.81270 — 2026-08-16",
    "highlights": [
      "A stop inside a multi-part section (the Confiteor within the prayers at the foot of the altar; the Alleluia verse within a Sunday Gradual) now lands on its own line even when that section started folded — the first release's landing worked only when the section was already open."
    ],
    "markdown": "Completes the stop-landing fix of v1.33.\n\n- A stop inside a multi-part section (the Confiteor within the prayers at the foot of the altar; the Alleluia verse within a Sunday Gradual) now lands on its own line even when that section started folded — the first release's landing worked only when the section was already open.\n\n### For maintainers\n\n- Root cause: a folded section renders no body, so the focus effect's line query ran before the unfold painted. Fix: retry the refinement after the unfold renders (double `requestAnimationFrame`) — `ReaderView` focus effect."
  },
